---
/**
 * K Culture Wire — **「underrated korean drama」를 자료로 답한다.** (`/underrated`)
 *
 * ── 왜 이 지면인가 (2026-08-22) ────────────────────────────────
 * 사장님: 「왜 너의 커뮤니티인데 케이라이프맵의 커뮤니티 같지? 수정하자...**검색량**」
 * 그래서 K컬처 후보 35개를 자동완성으로 쟀다. 「underrated korean drama」가
 * **1번째로 뜨고 그 말로 시작하는 제안이 9줄**이었다 —
 * romance / reddit / list / in netflix / 2025 / 2026 …
 *
 * ⭐ 그런데 이 말에 답하는 곳은 **전부 취향**이다. 「내가 좋아한 숨은 명작」 목록이다.
 *   우리는 셀 수 있다 — 넷플릭스 주간 10위, 93개국, 265주.
 *   **오래 갔는데 거의 아무 나라도 안 본 것**이 자료로 정의되는 「underrated」다.
 *
 * ── ⛔ 이 지면이 하지 않는 것 ─────────────────────────────────
 * ⛔ 「좋은 작품」이라고 하지 않는다. 우리가 판정할 자격이 없다.
 * ⛔ 차트에 든 것을 「볼 수 있다」로 바꿔 쓰지 않는다 — 넷플릭스는 제공 여부를 안 낸다.
 * ⛔ 차트에 안 든 것을 「안 봤다」로 바꿔 쓰지 않는다 — 10위 밖은 자료가 없다.
 * ⛔ 문턱을 취향으로 고르지 않는다. 주수는 중간값, 나라 수는 아래 사분위 —
 *   `build-kcw-quiet-hits.mjs` 가 잰 분포에서 가져온다.
 */
import WikiTip from '../../layouts/WikiTip.astro';
import KcwMethodLimits from '../../components/KcwMethodLimits.astro';
import data from '../../data/wikitip-quiet-hits.json';

const TITLE = 'Underrated Korean drama, measured instead of guessed';
const DESC = 'Korean series and films that stayed on a Netflix weekly top 10 for a long run while '
  + 'charting in only one or two countries. Both cut-offs come from the measured spread of every '
  + 'Korean title we hold, not from anybody’s taste.';

const 띠 = data.bands ?? [];
const 띠이름 = (b: { from: number; to: number }) => (b.from === b.to
  ? (b.from === 1 ? 'One country only' : `Exactly ${b.from} countries`)
  : `${b.from} to ${b.to} countries`);

const 총 = 띠.reduce((n, b) => n + b.titles.length, 0);

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Dataset',
  name: TITLE,
  description: DESC,
  temporalCoverage: `${data.weekFrom}/${data.weekTo}`,
  spatialCoverage: `${data.marketCount} countries`,
  creator: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'K Culture Wire' },
  isBasedOn: ['https://www.netflix.com/tudum/top10'],
};
---

<WikiTip title={TITLE} description={DESC} jsonLd={jsonLd} canonical="https://www.kculturewire.com/underrated">
  <h1>Underrated Korean drama, measured instead of guessed</h1>

  <p class="lead">
    Everybody&rsquo;s list of underrated Korean shows is somebody&rsquo;s taste. This one is a
    count. A title is here if it stayed on a Netflix weekly top 10 for
    <b>{data.thresholds.longRunWeeks} weeks or more</b> &mdash; the median run of the
    {data.pagesConsidered} titles we publish &mdash; while appearing in the charts of
    <b>fewer countries than most of them</b>. {총} titles do both.
  </p>

  <p class="warn">
    <b>This is not a claim that they are good.</b> It says a title kept its place somewhere for a
    long time and almost nowhere else noticed. Netflix publishes only the weekly top 10, so a show
    that is enormous at home can be missing from this page entirely, and charting somewhere is not
    the same as being available there.
  </p>

  {띠.map((b) => (
    <section>
      <h2>{띠이름(b)}</h2>
      <p class="sub">
        {b.titles.length} titles ran {data.thresholds.longRunWeeks} weeks or more and charted in{' '}
        {b.from === b.to ? `${b.from} ${b.from === 1 ? 'country' : 'countries'}` : `${b.from}–${b.to} countries`}.
      </p>
      {b.titles.length ? (
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Title</th><th>Kind</th><th class="num">Weeks</th><th>Where it charted</th><th class="num">Best place</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {b.titles.map((t) => (
              <tr>
                <td class="nm"><a href={`/title/${t.slug}`}>{t.title}</a></td>
                <td class="fine">{t.type === 'TV' ? 'Series' : 'Film'}</td>
                <td class="num">{t.weeks}</td>
                <td class="fine">{t.where.join(', ')}</td>
                <td class="num">{t.peak}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      ) : (
        <p class="fine">No title in our data falls in this band. That is a measured emptiness, not a gap.</p>
      )}
    </section>
  ))}

  <section>
    <h2>Series or film &mdash; the split</h2>
    <p class="sub">
      Of the titles that clear both cut-offs at the strictest band, {data.counts.tv} are series and
      {' '}{data.counts.film} are films. People search for the two separately, so we count them
      separately rather than folding them into one word.
    </p>
    <p class="fine">{data.whatThisIs}</p>
    <p class="fine"><b>What it is not.</b> {data.whatThisIsNot}</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>The other end &mdash; seen everywhere, gone in a fortnight</h2>
    <p class="sub">
      The same two measures, reversed: {data.counts.wideAndBrief} titles charted in
      {' '}{data.thresholds.wideCountries} countries or more and were gone within
      {' '}{data.thresholds.shortRunWeeks} weeks. Reach and staying power are not the same thing,
      and putting the two lists beside each other is what makes either one mean anything.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Title</th><th>Kind</th><th class="num">Countries</th><th class="num">Weeks</th><th class="num">Best place</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {data.wideAndBrief.map((t) => (
          <tr>
            <td class="nm"><a href={`/title/${t.slug}`}>{t.title}</a></td>
            <td class="fine">{t.type === 'TV' ? 'Series' : 'Film'}</td>
            <td class="num">{t.markets}</td>
            <td class="num">{t.weeks}</td>
            <td class="num">{t.peak}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Where to walk from here</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="/by-country">Every country and how Korean its chart is</a> &middot;{' '}
      <a href="/staying-power">Longest run against hardest landing</a> &middot;{' '}
      <a href="/titles">Every Korean title we hold</a> &middot;{' '}
      <a href="/community">All the rooms</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <KcwMethodLimits
    method={`Netflix's own weekly top 10 files, ${data.weekCount} weeks across ${data.marketCount} countries, ${data.weekFrom} to ${data.weekTo}. A title is counted here when its weeks on any weekly top 10 reach ${data.thresholds.longRunWeeks} — the median run of the ${data.pagesConsidered} titles that have a page on this site — and the number of countries it charted in stays below the median of ${data.medianCountries}. The first quartile of that country count is ${data.thresholds.fewCountries}, which is the band shown first. Neither cut-off was chosen by hand.`}
    limitation="Charting is not availability: Netflix does not publish where a title can be watched. Not charting is not the same as not being watched, because only the weekly top 10 is published, so a title that was enormous in Korea and never charted abroad does not appear here at all. Netflix also states no country of production, so which titles count as Korean is our inference and not its label."
    note="The same two measures build the opposite list on this page, and the country counts behind them are on the country pages."
  />

  <style>
    .lead { font-size: 1.06rem; }
    .warn { border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); padding: .7rem 1rem; margin: 1.4rem 0 2rem;
      font-size: .95rem; }
    h2 { font-size: 1.12rem; margin: 2.4rem 0 .3rem; }
    .sub { color: var(--muted); font-size: .92rem; margin: 0 0 .8rem; }
    table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: .92rem; }
    th, td { text-align: left; padding: .4rem .5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
    th.num, td.num { text-align: right; }
    .nm { font-weight: 600; }
    .fine { color: var(--muted); font-size: .86rem; }
  </style>
</WikiTip>
